# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5
# The deterministic properties with the lanes of the host pair rows
# (D[host-pair-vector]): the shipped default of the deterministic mode takes
# lanes(8) in f32 and lanes(4) in f64 on every host, while the suite pins
# MDIR_HOST_PAIRS=scalar, so the tests of these properties ran the scalar
# row. Here they run with MDIR_HOST_PAIRS unset, the default.
# The thermostats against mdir run, in parts and across a checkpoint in both
# directions (Inputs/python_thermostats.py, as python-thermostats-*.test).
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/mixed %t/double
# RUN: env -u MDIR_HOST_PAIRS %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_thermostats.py %S/Inputs CPU Mixed mdir %t/mixed cases | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MIXED
# RUN: env -u MDIR_HOST_PAIRS %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_thermostats.py %S/Inputs CPU Double mdir %t/double cases | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DOUBLE

# MIXED: thermostats CPU Mixed: 7 cases passed
# DOUBLE: thermostats CPU Double: 7 cases passed
